{"schema":1,"locale":"zh-Hans","created_at":"2026-11-28T11:21:55.997Z","entries":{"description:This page addresses Layer2 misconfigurations in MikroTik RouterOS, focusing on issues like improper bridge setups with hardware offloading and port isolation. It explains symptoms such as low throughput, high CPU usage, and incorrect hardware offloading flags, along with solutions for devices that lack port isolation support.":"本页介绍 MikroTik RouterOS 中的 Layer2 配置错误，重点说明硬件卸载和端口隔离相关的网桥配置不当问题。文中解释了低吞吐量、高 CPU 使用率以及硬件卸载标志不正确等症状，并提供了针对不支持端口隔离的设备的解决方案。","docs-7.24\u0000## caps-man/access-list **Package:** wireless-rep **Type:** Directory":"## caps-man/access-list \n**Package:** wireless-rep\n**Type:** 目录","docs-7.24\u0000## caps-man/actual-interface-configuration **Package:** wireless-rep **Type:** Directory":"## caps-man/actual-interface-configuration \n**包：** wireless-rep\n**类型：** 目录","docs-7.24\u0000## caps-man/channel **Package:** wireless-rep **Type:** Directory":"## caps-man/channel \n**Package:** wireless-rep\n**Type:** 目录","docs-7.24\u0000## caps-man/configuration **Package:** wireless-rep **Type:** Directory":"## caps-man/configuration \n**包：** wireless-rep\n**类型：** 目录","docs-7.24\u0000## caps-man/datapath **Package:** wireless-rep **Type:** Directory":"## caps-man/datapath \n**Package:** wireless-rep\n**Type:** 目录","docs-7.24\u0000## caps-man/interface/hw-info **Package:** wireless-rep **Type:** Command":"## caps-man/interface/hw-info \n**包：** wireless-rep\n**类型：** Command","docs-7.24\u0000## caps-man/interface/possible-channels **Package:** wireless-rep **Type:** Command":"## caps-man/interface/possible-channels \n**包：** wireless-rep\n**类型：** Command","docs-7.24\u0000## caps-man/interface/reselect-channel **Package:** wireless-rep **Type:** Command":"## caps-man/interface/reselect-channel \n**包：** wireless-rep\n**类型：** Command","docs-7.24\u0000## caps-man/interface/scan **Package:** wireless-rep **Type:** Command":"## caps-man/interface/scan \n**包：** wireless-rep\n**类型：** Command","docs-7.24\u0000### Interface Lists in VLAN Table":"### VLAN 表中的接口列表","docs-7.24\u0000:::info RouterOS can handle a maximum of 1024 bridged interfaces per bridge; this limit is fixed and cannot be modified. If you try to add more interfaces as bridge ports, it may lead to unpredictable behavior. :::":":::info\n每个网桥最多可处理 1024 个桥接接口；此限制是固定的，无法修改。如果尝试添加更多接口作为网桥端口，可能会导致不可预测的行为。\n:::","docs-7.24\u0000:::warning When using the `move` command, the second parameter represents the \"before id\" position, which determines where the selected interface list will be moved. If the first interface list is moved to the position of the second interface list, the command has no effect since the first list would already be positioned before the second list. :::":":::warning\n使用 `move` 命令时，第二个参数表示“before id”位置，用于确定所选接口列表将移动到的位置。如果将第一个接口列表移动到第二个接口列表的位置，该命令不会产生效果，因为第一个列表已经位于第二个列表之前。\n:::","docs-7.24\u0000First, add each port to the bridge interface:":"首先，将每个端口添加到网桥接口：","docs-7.24\u0000Starting from RouterOS version 7.17, you can use interface lists for the `tagged` and `untagged` properties in the bridge VLAN table. This enhancement allows for more flexible VLAN assignment to ports by simply modifying the interface list members, rather than updating each bridge VLAN entry individually.":"从 RouterOS 7.17 版本开始，可以在网桥 VLAN 表的 `tagged` 和 `untagged` 属性中使用接口列表。此增强功能允许通过修改接口列表成员来更灵活地为端口分配 VLAN，而无需逐个更新网桥 VLAN 条目。","docs-7.24\u0000Starting with RouterOS v6.41, interface lists can be added as bridge ports and sorted. Interface lists simplify firewall rule configuration by grouping multiple interfaces together. The following example demonstrates how to add an interface list to a bridge:":"从 RouterOS v6.41 开始，接口列表可以作为网桥端口添加并进行排序。接口列表通过将多个接口分组，简化防火墙规则配置。以下示例演示如何向网桥添加接口列表：","docs-7.24\u0000The Port submenu is used to add interfaces in a particular bridge.":"Port 子菜单用于在指定网桥中添加接口。","docs-7.24\u0000The order in which interface lists appear can be rearranged using the `move` command. The second parameter specifies the position before which the selected interface list should be placed. The following example demonstrates how to sort interface lists:":"可以使用 `move` 命令调整接口列表的显示顺序。第二个参数指定所选接口列表应放置的位置，即位于该位置之前。以下示例演示如何对接口列表排序：","docs-7.24\u0000The output confirms both ports are now bridged together. The **H** flag indicates that hardware offloading is active, meaning the switch chip is handling packet forwarding for optimal performance. Each port is assigned a default PVID(Port VLAN ID) of 100 and 200 respectively, and both use the standard STP priority of 0x80.":"输出确认两个端口现已加入同一网桥。**H** 标志表示硬件卸载已启用，即交换芯片正在处理数据包转发，以获得最佳性能。每个端口分别分配了默认 PVID（Port VLAN ID）100 和 200，并且均使用标准 STP 优先级 0x80。","docs-7.24\u0000This example demonstrates how to add Ethernet ports to an existing bridge interface to create a simple Layer 2 switching setup. By adding **ether1** and **ether2** to **bridge1**, these physical ports become part of a single switched network segment, allowing devices connected to either port to communicate with each other as if they were on the same LAN.":"本示例演示如何向现有网桥接口添加以太网端口，以创建简单的 Layer 2 交换配置。通过将 **ether1** 和 **ether2** 添加到 **bridge1**，这些物理端口将成为单个交换网络网段的一部分，使连接到任一端口的设备能够相互通信，就像它们位于同一 LAN 中一样。","docs-7.24\u0000Verify the configuration by displaying the bridge port table:":"通过显示网桥端口表验证配置：","docs-7.24\u0000When interface lists are added to a bridge, the individual ports from those lists appear as dynamic ports entries:":"将接口列表添加到网桥后，这些列表中的各个端口会显示为动态端口条目：","docs-7.24\u0000You should only use supported SFP modules. Always check the [SFP compatibility table](LINK) if you are intending to use SFP modules manufactured by MikroTik. There are other SFP modules that do work with MikroTik devices as well. Check the [Supported peripherals table](LINK) to find other SFP modules that have been confirmed to work with MikroTik devices. Some unsupported modules might not be working properly at certain speeds and with auto-negotiation. You might want to try to disable it and manually set a link speed.":"请仅使用受支持的 SFP 模块。如果打算使用 MikroTik 生产的 SFP 模块，请始终查看 [SFP compatibility table](/docs/7.24/wired-connections/mikrotik-wired-interface-compatibility)。其他 SFP 模块也可与 MikroTik 设备配合使用。请查看 [Supported peripherals table](/docs/7.24/hardware/peripherals#sfp-modules)，查找已确认可与 MikroTik 设备配合使用的其他 SFP 模块。某些不受支持的模块在特定速率和自动协商下可能无法正常工作。可以尝试禁用自动协商，并手动设置链路速率。","docs-7.24\u0000| Property | Description | | :-- | :-- | | **auto-isolate**(*yes \\| no*; Default: **no**) | When enabled, it prevents a port from moving from discarding state into forwarding state if no BPDUs are received from the neighboring bridge. The port will change into a forwarding state only when a BPDU is received. This property only has an effect when `protocol-mode` is set to `rstp` or `mstp` and `edge` is set to `no`. | | **bpdu-guard**(*yes \\| no*; Default: **no**) | Enables or disables the BPDU Guard feature on a port. This feature puts the port in a disabled role if it receives a BPDU and requires the port to be manually disabled and enabled if a BPDU is received. It should be used to prevent a bridge from BPDU-related attacks. This property has no effect when `protocol-mode` is set to `none`. | | **bridge**(*name*; Default: **none**) | The bridge interface where the respective interface is grouped. | | **broadcast-flood**(*yes \\| no*; Default: **yes**) | When enabled, the bridge floods broadcast traffic to all bridge egress ports. When disabled, the bridge drops broadcast traffic on egress ports. It can be used to filter all broadcast traffic on an egress port. Broadcast traffic is considered as traffic that uses **FF:FF:FF:FF:FF:FF** as the destination MAC address. Such traffic is crucial for many protocols such as DHCP, ARP, NDP, BOOTP(Netinstall), and others. This option does not limit traffic flood to the CPU. | | **edge**(*auto \\| no \\| no-discover \\| yes \\| yes-discover*; Default: **auto**) | Set a port as an edge port or a non-edge port, or enable edge discovery. Edge ports are connected to a LAN that has no other bridges attached. An edge port will skip the learning and the listening states in STP and will transition directly to the forwarding state. This reduces the STP initialization time. If the port is configured to discover an edge port, then as soon as the bridge detects a BPDU coming to an edge port, the port becomes a non-edge port. This property has no effect when <code>protocol-mode</code> is set to <code>none</code>.<ul><li><span className=\"ros-icon-success\"><code>no</code></span> - non-edge port with disabled discovery. It will participate in learning and listening states in STP. It will not transition to the forwarding state until it exchanges BPDUs and reaches agreement with the connected bridge. If no BPDU is received, the port may remain in a non-forwarding state indefinitely.</li><li><span className=\"ros-icon-success\"><code>no-discover</code></span> - non-edge port with enabled discovery. It will participate in learning and listening states in STP. A port can become an edge port if no BPDU is received.</li><li><span className=\"ros-icon-success\"><code>yes</code></span> - edge port without discovery. It will transition directly to forwarding state.</li><li><span className=\"ros-icon-success\"><code>yes-discover</code></span> - edge port with enabled discovery. It will transition directly to forwarding state.</li><li><span className=\"ros-icon-success\"><code>auto</code></span> - same as <span className=\"ros-icon-success\"><code>no-discover</code></span>, but will additionally detect if a bridge port is a Wireless interface with disabled bridge-mode. Such an interface will be automatically set as an edge port without discovery.</li></ul> | | **fast-leave**(*yes \\| no*; Default: **no**) | Enables the IGMP/MLD fast leave feature on the bridge port. The bridge will stop forwarding multicast traffic to a bridge port when an IGMP/MLD leave message is received. This property only has an effect when `igmp-snooping` is set to `yes`. | | **frame-types**(*admit-all \\| admit-only-untagged-and-priority-tagged \\| admit-only-vlan-tagged*; Default: **admit-all**) | Specifies allowed ingress frame types on a bridge port. This property only has an effect when `vlan-filtering` is set to `yes`. | | **ingress-filtering**(*yes \\| no*; Default: **yes**) | Enables or disables VLAN ingress filtering, which checks if the ingress port is a member of the received VLAN ID in the bridge VLAN table. Should be used with `frame-types` to specify if the ingress traffic should be tagged or untagged. This property only has an effect when `vlan-filtering` is set to `yes`. The setting is enabled by default since RouterOS v7. | | **learn**(*auto \\| no \\| yes*; Default: **auto**) | Changes MAC learning behavior on a bridge port<ul><li><span className=\"ros-icon-success\"><code>yes</code></span> - enables MAC learning</li><li><span className=\"ros-icon-success\"><code>no</code></span> - disables MAC learning</li><li><span className=\"ros-icon-success\"><code>auto</code></span> - detects if the bridge port is a Wireless interface and uses a Wireless registration table instead of MAC learning, will use the Wireless registration table if the Wireless interface is set to one of <span className=\"ros-icon-success\"><code>ap-bridge</code></span>, <span className=\"ros-icon-success\"><code>bridge</code></span>, <span className=\"ros-icon-success\"><code>wds-slave</code></span> mode and bridge mode for the Wireless interface is disabled.</li></ul> | | **multicast-router**(*disabled \\| permanent \\| temporary-query*; Default: **temporary-query**) | A multicast router port is a port where a multicast router or querier is connected. On this port, unregistered multicast streams and IGMP/MLD membership reports will be sent. This setting changes the state of the multicast router for bridge ports. This property can be used to send IGMP/MLD membership reports to certain bridge ports for further multicast routing or proxying. This property only has an effect when <code>igmp-snooping</code> is set to <span className=\"ros-icon-success\"><code>yes</code></span>.<ul><li><span className=\"ros-icon-success\"><code>disabled</code></span> - disabled multicast router state on the bridge port. Unregistered multicast and IGMP/MLD membership reports are not sent to the bridge port regardless of what is connected to it.</li><li><span className=\"ros-icon-success\"><code>permanent</code></span> - enabled multicast router state on the bridge port. Unregistered multicast and IGMP/MLD membership reports are sent to the bridge port regardless of what is connected to it.</li><li><span className=\"ros-icon-success\"><code>temporary-query</code></span> - automatically detect multicast router state on the bridge port using IGMP/MLD queries.</li></ul> | | **horizon**(*integer 0..429496729*; Default: **none**) | Use split horizon bridging to prevent bridging loops. Set the same value for a group of ports, to prevent them from sending data to ports with the same horizon value. Split horizon is a software feature that disables hardware offloading. | | **hw**(*yes \\| no*; Default: **yes**) | Allows enabling or disabling [hardware offloading](LINK) on interfaces capable of HW offloading. For software interfaces like [EoIP](LINK) or [VLAN](LINK), this setting is ignored and has no effect. Certain bridge or port functions can automatically disable HW offloading, use the `print` command to see whether the \"H\" flag is active. | | **internal-path-cost**(*integer: 1..200000000*; Default:) | Path cost to the interface for MSTI0 inside a region. If not manually configured, the bridge automatically determines the internal-path-cost based on the interface speed and the <code>port-cost-mode</code> setting. To revert to the automatic determination and remove any manually applied value, simply use an exclamation mark before the <code>internal-path-cost</code> property. This property only has an effect when <code>protocol-mode</code> is set to <code>mstp</code>. <br/><code>/interface/bridge/port/set [find interface=sfp28-1] !internal-path-cost</code> Use <a href=\"LINK\">port monitor</a> to observe the applied internal-path-cost. <br/> | | **interface**(*name*; Default: **none**) | Name of the interface or interface list. | | **path-cost**(*integer: 1..200000000*; Default:) | Path cost to the interface, used by STP and RSTP to determine the best path, and used by MSTP to determine the best path between regions. If not manually configured, the bridge automatically determines the path-cost based on the interface speed and the <code>port-cost-mode</code> setting. To revert to the automatic determination and remove any manually applied value, simply use an exclamation mark before the <code>path-cost</code> property. This property has no effect when <code>protocol-mode</code> is set to <code>none</code>. <br/><code>/interface/bridge/port/set [find interface=sfp28-1] !path-cost</code> Use <a href=\"LINK\">port monitor</a> to observe the applied path-cost. <br/> | | **point-to-point**(*auto \\| yes \\| no*; Default: **auto**) | Specifies if a bridge port is connected to a bridge using a point-to-point link for faster convergence in case of failure. By setting this property to `yes`, you are forcing the link to be a point-to-point link, which will skip the checking mechanism, which detects and waits for BPDUs from other devices on this single link. By setting this property to `no`, you are expecting that a link can receive BPDUs from multiple devices. By setting the property to `yes`, you are significantly improving(R/M)STP convergence time. In general, you should only set this property to `no` if it is possible that another device can be connected to a link. This is mostly relevant to Wireless mediums and Ethernet hubs. If the Ethernet link is full-duplex, `auto` enables point-to-point functionality. This property has no effect when `protocol-mode` is set to `none`. | | **priority**(*0x00 \\| 0x10 \\| 0x20 \\| 0x30 \\| 0x40 \\| 0x50 \\| 0x60 \\| 0x70 \\| 0x80 \\| 0x90 \\| 0xa0 \\| 0xb0 \\| 0xc0 \\| 0xd0 \\| 0xe0 \\| 0xf0*; Default: **0x80**) | The priority of the interface, used by STP to determine the root port, used by MSTP to determine the root port between regions. Must be set in steps of 16(0x10). | | **pvid**(*integer 1..4094*; Default: **1**) | Port VLAN ID(pvid) specifies which VLAN the untagged ingress traffic is assigned to. This property only has an effect when `vlan-filtering` is set to `yes`. | | **restricted-role**(*yes \\| no*; Default: **no**) | Enables or disables the restricted role on a port. When enabled, it prevents the port from becoming the root port for the CIST or any MSTI, regardless of its best spanning tree priority vector. Such a port will be selected as an Alternate Port(discarding state) and remains so as long as it continues to receive superior BPDUs. It will automatically transition to the forwarding state when it no longer detects a superior root path. Network administrators may enable this setting to safeguard against external bridges influencing the active spanning tree, a feature also known as root-guard or root-protection. This property has an effect when `protocol-mode` is set to `stp`, `rstp`, or `mstp`(support for STP and RSTP is available since RouterOS v7.14). | | **restricted-tcn**(*yes \\| no*; Default: **no**) | Enables or disables topology change notification(TCN) handling on a port. When enabled, it causes the port not to propagate received topology change notifications to other ports, and any changes caused by the port itself do not result in topology change notification to other ports. This parameter is disabled by default. It can be set by a network administrator to prevent external bridges from causing MAC address flushing in the local network. This property has an effect when `protocol-mode` is set to `stp`, `rstp`, or `mstp`(support for STP and RSTP is available since RouterOS v7.14). | | **tag-stacking**(*yes \\| no*; Default: **no**) | Forces all packets to be treated as untagged packets. Packets on the ingress port will be tagged with another VLAN tag regardless of whether a VLAN tag already exists. Packets will be tagged with a VLAN ID that matches the `pvid`value and will use EtherType that is specified in `ether-type`. This property only has an effect when `vlan-filtering` is set to `yes`. | | **trusted**(*yes \\| no*; Default: **no**) | When enabled, it allows forwarding DHCP packets towards the DHCP server through this port. Mainly used to prevent unauthorized servers from providing malicious information for users. This property only has an effect when `dhcp-snooping` is set to `yes`. | | **trusted-dhcpv6**(*yes \\| no*; Default: **no**) | When enabled, it allows forwarding DHCPv6 packets towards the DHCP server through this port. Mainly used to prevent unauthorized servers from providing malicious information for users. This property only has an effect when `dhcpv6-snooping` is set to `yes`. | | **trusted-ra**(*yes \\| no*; Default: **no**) | Specifies whether the port is permitted to forward IPv6 Router Advertisement messages; set to **yes** for ports connected to legitimate routers and **no** to block unauthorized sources. This property only has an effect when `ra-guard` is set to `yes`. | | **unknown-multicast-flood**(*yes \\| no*; Default: **yes**) | Changes the multicast flood option on the bridge port and only controls the egress traffic. When enabled, the bridge allows flooding multicast packets to the specified bridge port, but when disabled, the bridge restricts multicast traffic from being flooded to the specified bridge port. The setting affects all multicast traffic. This includes non-IP, IPv4, IPv6 and the link-local multicast ranges(e.g. 224.0.0.0/24 and ff02::1). <br/> Note that when <code>igmp-snooping</code> is enabled and an IGMP/MLD querier is detected, the bridge will automatically restrict unknown IP multicast from being flooded, so the setting is not mandatory for IGMP/MLD snooping setups. <br/> When using this setting together with <code>igmp-snooping</code>, the only multicast traffic that is allowed on the bridge port is the known multicast from the MDB table. | | **unknown-unicast-flood**(*yes \\| no*; Default: **yes**) | Changes the unknown unicast flood option on the bridge port and only controls the egress traffic. When enabled, the bridge allows flooding unknown unicast packets to the specified bridge port, but when disabled, the bridge restricts unknown unicast traffic from being flooded to the specified bridge port. <br/> If a MAC address is not learned in the host table, then the traffic is considered unknown unicast traffic and will be flooded to all ports. MAC address is learned as soon as a packet on a bridge port is received and the source MAC address is added to the bridge host table. Since it is required for the bridge to receive at least one packet on the bridge port to learn the MAC address, it is recommended to use static bridge host entries to avoid packets being dropped until the MAC address has been learned. |":"| 属性 | 说明 |\n| :-- | :-- |\n| **auto-isolate** (*yes \\| no*；默认值：**no**) | 启用后，如果未从相邻网桥收到 BPDU，则会阻止端口从丢弃状态切换到转发状态。只有在收到 BPDU 后，端口才会切换为转发状态。仅当 `protocol-mode` 设置为 `rstp` 或 `mstp` 且 `edge` 设置为 `no` 时，该属性才生效。 |\n| **bpdu-guard** (*yes \\| no*；默认值：**no**) | 启用或禁用端口上的 BPDU Guard 功能。如果端口收到 BPDU，该功能会将端口置于禁用角色，并且需要手动禁用和启用端口。应使用此功能防止网桥受到与 BPDU 相关的攻击。当 `protocol-mode` 设置为 `none` 时，该属性无效。 |\n| **bridge** (*name*；默认值：**none**) | 相应接口所属分组的网桥接口。 |\n| **broadcast-flood** (*yes \\| no*；默认值：**yes**) | 启用后，网桥会将广播流量泛洪到所有网桥出口端口。禁用后，网桥会在出口端口丢弃广播流量。可使用此属性过滤出口端口上的所有广播流量。广播流量被视为使用 **FF:FF:FF:FF:FF:FF** 作为目标 MAC 地址的流量。此类流量对 DHCP、ARP、NDP、BOOTP（Netinstall）等许多协议至关重要。此选项不限制泛洪到 CPU 的流量。 |\n| **edge** (*auto \\| no \\| no-discover \\| yes \\| yes-discover*；默认值：**auto**) | 将端口设置为边缘端口或非边缘端口，或启用边缘发现。边缘端口连接到没有其他网桥的 LAN。边缘端口会跳过 STP 中的学习和侦听状态，直接切换到转发状态。这会缩短 STP 初始化时间。如果端口配置为发现边缘端口，则当网桥检测到 BPDU 到达边缘端口时，该端口将成为非边缘端口。当 <code>protocol-mode</code> 设置为 <code>none</code> 时，该属性无效。<ul><li><span className=\"ros-icon-success\"><code>no</code></span> - 禁用发现的边缘端口。它将参与 STP 中的学习和侦听状态。在与相连网桥交换 BPDU 并达成一致之前，它不会切换到转发状态。如果未收到 BPDU，该端口可能无限期保持非转发状态。</li><li><span className=\"ros-icon-success\"><code>no-discover</code></span> - 启用发现的非边缘端口。它将参与 STP 中的学习和侦听状态。如果未收到 BPDU，端口可以成为边缘端口。</li><li><span className=\"ros-icon-success\"><code>yes</code></span> - 不带发现的边缘端口。它将直接切换到转发状态。</li><li><span className=\"ros-icon-success\"><code>yes-discover</code></span> - 启用发现的边缘端口。它将直接切换到转发状态。</li><li><span className=\"ros-icon-success\"><code>auto</code></span> - 与 <span className=\"ros-icon-success\"><code>no-discover</code></span> 相同，但还会检测网桥端口是否为禁用 bridge-mode 的 Wireless 接口。此类接口将自动设置为不带发现的边缘端口。</li></ul> |\n| **fast-leave** (*yes \\| no*；默认值：**no**) | 在网桥端口上启用 IGMP/MLD fast leave 功能。收到 IGMP/MLD leave 消息后，网桥将停止向该网桥端口转发组播流量。仅当 `igmp-snooping` 设置为 `yes` 时，该属性才生效。 |\n| **frame-types** (*admit-all \\| admit-only-untagged-and-priority-tagged \\| admit-only-vlan-tagged*；默认值：**admit-all**) | 指定网桥端口上允许的入站帧类型。仅当 `vlan-filtering` 设置为 `yes` 时，该属性才生效。 |\n| **ingress-filtering** (*yes \\| no*；默认值：**yes**) | 启用或禁用 VLAN 入站过滤，该过滤会检查入站端口是否为网桥 VLAN 表中所接收 VLAN ID 的成员。应与 `frame-types` 一起使用，以指定入站流量应带标签还是不带标签。仅当 `vlan-filtering` 设置为 `yes` 时，该属性才生效。自 RouterOS v7 起，该设置默认启用。 |\n| **learn** (*auto \\| no \\| yes*；默认值：**auto**) | 更改网桥端口上的 MAC 学习行为<ul><li><span className=\"ros-icon-success\"><code>yes</code></span> - 启用 MAC 学习</li><li><span className=\"ros-icon-success\"><code>no</code></span> - 禁用 MAC 学习</li><li><span className=\"ros-icon-success\"><code>auto</code></span> - 检测网桥端口是否为 Wireless 接口，并使用 Wireless 注册表代替 MAC 学习；当 Wireless 接口设置为 <span className=\"ros-icon-success\"><code>ap-bridge</code></span>、<span className=\"ros-icon-success\"><code>bridge</code></span>、<span className=\"ros-icon-success\"><code>wds-slave</code></span> 模式之一且该 Wireless 接口的 bridge mode 已禁用时，将使用 Wireless 注册表。</li></ul> |\n| **multicast-router** (*disabled \\| permanent \\| temporary-query*；默认值：**temporary-query**) | 组播路由器端口是连接组播路由器或查询器的端口。在该端口上，将发送未注册的组播流和 IGMP/MLD 成员报告。此设置会更改网桥端口的组播路由器状态。可使用该属性将 IGMP/MLD 成员报告发送到指定网桥端口，以便进一步进行组播路由或代理。仅当 <code>igmp-snooping</code> 设置为 <span className=\"ros-icon-success\"><code>yes</code></span> 时，该属性才生效。<ul><li><span className=\"ros-icon-success\"><code>disabled</code></span> - 在网桥端口上禁用组播路由器状态。无论连接了什么设备，未注册组播和 IGMP/MLD 成员报告都不会发送到该网桥端口。</li><li><span className=\"ros-icon-success\"><code>permanent</code></span> - 在网桥端口上启用组播路由器状态。无论连接了什么设备，未注册组播和 IGMP/MLD 成员报告都会发送到该网桥端口。</li><li><span className=\"ros-icon-success\"><code>temporary-query</code></span> - 使用 IGMP/MLD 查询自动检测网桥端口上的组播路由器状态。</li></ul> |\n| **horizon** (*integer 0..429496729*；默认值：**none**) | 使用水平分割网桥防止网桥环路。为一组端口设置相同的值，以防止它们向具有相同 horizon 值的端口发送数据。水平分割是软件功能，会禁用硬件卸载。 |\n| **hw** (*yes \\| no*；默认值：**yes**) | 允许在支持 HW 卸载的接口上启用或禁用[硬件卸载](/docs/7.24/bridging-and-switching#bridge-hardware-offloading)。对于软件接口，例如 [EoIP](/docs/virtual-private-networks/eoip) 或 [VLAN](/docs/7.24/vlan)，此设置会被忽略且无效。某些网桥或端口功能会自动禁用 HW 卸载，可使用 `print` 命令查看“H”标志是否处于活动状态。 |\n| **internal-path-cost** (*integer: 1..200000000*；默认值：) | 区域内 MSTI0 到该接口的路径开销。如果未手动配置，网桥会根据接口速度和 <code>port-cost-mode</code> 设置自动确定 internal-path-cost。要恢复自动确定并移除任何手动应用的值，只需在 <code>internal-path-cost</code> 属性前使用感叹号。仅当 <code>protocol-mode</code> 设置为 <code>mstp</code> 时，该属性才生效。 <br/><code>/interface/bridge/port/set [find interface=sfp28-1] !internal-path-cost</code> 使用 <a href=\"/docs/7.24/bridging-and-switching#bridge-port-monitoring\">端口监控</a> 查看已应用的 internal-path-cost。 <br/> |\n| **interface** (*name*；默认值：**none**) | 接口或接口列表的名称。 |\n| **path-cost** (*integer: 1..200000000*；默认值：) | 到接口的路径开销，STP 和 RSTP 使用它确定最佳路径，MSTP 使用它确定区域之间的最佳路径。如果未手动配置，网桥会根据接口速度和 <code>port-cost-mode</code> 设置自动确定 path-cost。要恢复自动确定并移除任何手动应用的值，只需在 <code>path-cost</code> 属性前使用感叹号。当 <code>protocol-mode</code> 设置为 <code>none</code> 时，该属性无效。 <br/><code>/interface/bridge/port/set [find interface=sfp28-1] !path-cost</code> 使用 <a href=\"/docs/7.24/bridging-and-switching#bridge-port-monitoring\">端口监控</a> 查看已应用的 path-cost。 <br/> |\n| **point-to-point** (*auto \\| yes \\| no*；默认值：**auto**) | 指定网桥端口是否通过点到点链路连接到网桥，以便在故障时更快收敛。将此属性设置为 `yes` 会强制链路为点到点链路，从而跳过检测机制，该机制会检测并等待该单条链路上其他设备的 BPDU。将此属性设置为 `no` 表示预期链路可能会收到多个设备的 BPDU。将属性设置为 `yes` 可显著改善 (R/M)STP 收敛时间。通常，只有在链路上可能连接其他设备时，才应将此属性设置为 `no`。这主要与 Wireless 介质和以太网集线器相关。如果以太网链路为全双工，`auto` 会启用点到点功能。当 `protocol-mode` 设置为 `none` 时，该属性无效。 |\n| **priority** (*0x00 \\| 0x10 \\| 0x20 \\| 0x30 \\| 0x40 \\| 0x50 \\| 0x60 \\| 0x70 \\| 0x80 \\| 0x90 \\| 0xa0 \\| 0xb0 \\| 0xc0 \\| 0xd0 \\| 0xe0 \\| 0xf0*；默认值：**0x80**) | 接口的优先级，STP 使用它确定根端口，MSTP 使用它确定区域之间的根端口。必须以 16（0x10）为步长设置。 |\n| **pvid** (*integer 1..4094*；默认值：**1**) | 端口 VLAN ID（pvid）指定将不带标签的入站流量分配到哪个 VLAN。仅当 `vlan-filtering` 设置为 `yes` 时，该属性才生效。 |\n| **restricted-role** (*yes \\| no*；默认值：**no**) | 启用或禁用端口上的受限角色。启用后，无论其生成树优先级向量是否最佳，都会阻止该端口成为 CIST 或任何 MSTI 的根端口。该端口将被选为 Alternate Port（丢弃状态），并在持续收到更优 BPDU 时保持该状态。当不再检测到更优根路径时，它将自动切换到转发状态。网络管理员可启用此设置，防止外部网桥影响活动生成树，该功能也称为 root-guard 或 root-protection。当 `protocol-mode` 设置为 `stp`、`rstp` 或 `mstp` 时，该属性生效（自 RouterOS v7.14 起支持 STP 和 RSTP）。 |\n| **restricted-tcn** (*yes \\| no*；默认值：**no**) | 启用或禁用端口上的拓扑变化通知（TCN）处理。启用后，该端口不会将收到的拓扑变化通知传播到其他端口，并且由该端口自身引起的任何变化也不会导致向其他端口发送拓扑变化通知。此参数默认禁用。网络管理员可设置此参数，防止外部网桥导致本地网络中的 MAC 地址刷新。当 `protocol-mode` 设置为 `stp`、`rstp` 或 `mstp` 时，该属性生效（自 RouterOS v7.14 起支持 STP 和 RSTP）。 |\n| **tag-stacking** (*yes \\| no*；默认值：**no**) | 强制所有数据包被视为不带标签的数据包。入站端口上的数据包将添加另一个 VLAN 标签，无论是否已存在 VLAN 标签。数据包将使用与 `pvid` 值匹配的 VLAN ID 添加标签，并使用 `ether-type` 中指定的 EtherType。仅当 `vlan-filtering` 设置为 `yes` 时，该属性才生效。 |\n| **trusted** (*yes \\| no*；默认值：**no**) | 启用后，允许通过该端口向 DHCP 服务器转发 DHCP 数据包。主要用于防止未经授权的服务器向用户提供恶意信息。仅当 `dhcp-snooping` 设置为 `yes` 时，该属性才生效。 |\n| **trusted-dhcpv6**(*yes \\| no*；默认值：**no**) | 启用后，允许通过该端口向 DHCP 服务器转发 DHCPv6 数据包。主要用于防止未经授权的服务器向用户提供恶意信息。仅当 `dhcpv6-snooping` 设置为 `yes` 时，该属性才生效。 |\n| **trusted-ra** (*yes \\| no*；默认值：**no**) | 指定是否允许该端口转发 IPv6 Router Advertisement 消息；对连接到合法路由器的端口设置为 **yes**，对阻止未授权来源的端口设置为 **no**。仅当 `ra-guard` 设置为 `yes` 时，该属性才生效。 |\n| **unknown-multicast-flood** (*yes \\| no*；默认值：**yes**) | 更改网桥端口上的组播泛洪选项，仅控制出口流量。启用后，网桥允许将组播数据包泛洪到指定网桥端口；禁用后，网桥限制组播流量泛洪到指定网桥端口。该设置影响所有组播流量，包括非 IP、IPv4、IPv6 和链路本地组播范围（例如 224.0.0.0/24 和 ff02::1）。 <br/> 请注意，当 <code>igmp-snooping</code> 已启用且检测到 IGMP/MLD 查询器时，网桥将自动限制未知 IP 组播的泛洪，因此对于 IGMP/MLD snooping 配置而言，该设置并非必需。 <br/> 将此设置与 <code>igmp-snooping</code> 一起使用时，网桥端口上唯一允许的组播流量是 MDB 表中的已知组播。 |\n| **unknown-unicast-flood** (*yes \\| no*；默认值：**yes**) | 更改网桥端口上的未知单播泛洪选项，仅控制出口流量。启用后，网桥允许将未知单播数据包泛洪到指定网桥端口；禁用后，网桥限制未知单播流量泛洪到指定网桥端口。 <br/> 如果 MAC 地址未在主机表中学习到，则该流量被视为未知单播流量，并将泛洪到所有端口。当网桥端口收到数据包且源 MAC 地址被添加到网桥主机表时，即完成 MAC 地址学习。由于网桥需要在网桥端口上至少收到一个数据包才能学习 MAC 地址，建议使用静态网桥主机条目，以避免在 MAC 地址学习完成前丢弃数据包。 |","title:Layer2 misconfiguration":"二层配置错误"}}
